Tests
ctest runs build/<Config>/MemoLangTests once per file.
Folder
What it checks
tests/ast/*.memo
Parses with no errors; --dump-ast output must equal the .ast file next to it
tests/tokens/*.memo
Lexes with no errors; token list must equal the .tokens file
tests/errors/*.memo
Parse errors: every error matches an # expect-error: <col>: <text> comment on its line (or # expect-error@+N: for N lines below), and there are no other errors
tests/check/*.memo
The whole front-end (parse, semantic and consumption analysis), with the same # expect-error comments. A file with none must come through with no errors
tests/run/*.memo
Runs main() with and without destructive reads: both must return the same value (# expect-result: <value>) or fail with # expect-runtime-error: <text>, and both must free every matrix
benchmarks/*.memo
The same check for each benchmark program
stress (built in)
Empty/huge/1 MB inputs, NUL bytes, CRLF, 100000-deep nesting of every kind, 10000-term chains (also through the analyses), 100 nested loops, throughput
fuzz (built in)
9000 random, token-soup and mutated inputs through every stage: no crash, no hang, same result every run
To add a test, drop a .memo file in the right folder and re-run CMake. For ast/tokens, the first run creates the expected-output file and fails until you have reviewed it. After an intended output change, regenerate it with MemoLangTests ast tests/ast/<name>.memo --update and check the diff.
